# What a HADES ingest of this workspace does not read.
#
# **A workspace declares its own exclusions.** The ingest is configured on the
# server and the corpus lives here, so a rule kept only on the server is a
# rule the tree cannot be checked against. Per issue #565.
#
# Syntax follows .gitignore: one pattern per line, `#` comments, `/` anchors
# to this file's directory, a trailing `/` matches directories only.

# Version control, environments, build products. Not the corpus.
.git/
.venv/
venv/
__pycache__/
target/
node_modules/

# **Frozen copies of live code.** An ingest walking one puts the same symbols
# in twice under two paths, so symbol resolution has two answers and no basis
# for choosing, and retrieval returns the stale text as readily as the live.
#
# The standing rule of 2026-09-13 is that git is the archive and no archive
# directory stands in this tree at all - the two that did were deleted at PR
# #563 and `census.py`'s `archive_directories` reading holds that at zero.
# **This entry is the second half of that rule and not a substitute for it**:
# a directory that reappears is caught by the census on the day it appears,
# and is excluded here in the window before someone acts on the finding.
**/archive/

# **Experiments are a separate corpus and leave this tree.** They record dated
# facts about runs against particular commits, where everything else here
# describes what the instrument currently is - so the two want edges to
# different things and an ingest that treats them alike answers confidently
# that an old result is about today's code. Per issue #564.
experiments/
